{"headword":"נִדָּה","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.f. impurity (</strong>as <em>abhorrent, shunned</em><strong>)</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">נ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 18:6\" href=\"/Ezekiel.18.6\">Ez 18:6</a> +; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">נִדַּת</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 12:2\" href=\"/Leviticus.12.2\">Lv 12:2</a> +; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">נִדָּתָהּ</span> v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 12:5\" href=\"/Leviticus.12.5\">5</a> +;—<em>impurity</em> (especially P and Ezek.):"},{"senses":[{"definition":"of ceremonial impurity, as union with brother’s wife, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 20:21\" href=\"/Leviticus.20.21\">Lv 20:21</a>; especially of menstruation <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 18:6\" href=\"/Ezekiel.18.6\">Ez 18:6</a> (read <span dir=\"rtl\">אִשָּׁה בְּנִדָּתָהּ</span> for MT <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳ נִדָּה</span> 𝔖 Co), <span dir=\"rtl\">טְמֵאַת הַנּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 22:10\" href=\"/Ezekiel.22.10\">22:10</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 36:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.36.17\">36:17</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">נִדַּת דְּוֹתָהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 12:2\" href=\"/Leviticus.12.2\">Lv 12:2</a>, cf. v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 12:5\" href=\"/Leviticus.12.5\">5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 15:19\" href=\"/Leviticus.15.19\">15:19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 15:20\" href=\"/Leviticus.15.20\">20</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 15:24\" href=\"/Leviticus.15.24\">24</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 15:25\" href=\"/Leviticus.15.25\">25</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(עֶת־נִדּ׳)</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 15:25\" href=\"/Leviticus.15.25\">25</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 15:26\" href=\"/Leviticus.15.26\">26</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(מִשְׁכַּב נִדּ׳)</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 15:26\" href=\"/Leviticus.15.26\">26</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(טֻמְאַת נִדּ׳)</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 15:33\" href=\"/Leviticus.15.33\">33</a>; <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 18:19\" href=\"/Leviticus.18.19\">18:19</a>; of defilement contracted by contact with a corpse, <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵי (הַ)נִּדָּה</span> <em>water of impurity</em> (i.e. to remove it, cf. Di) <a data-ref=\"Numbers 19:9\" href=\"/Numbers.19.9\">Nu 19:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 19:13\" href=\"/Numbers.19.13\">13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 19:20\" href=\"/Numbers.19.20\">20</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 19:21\" href=\"/Numbers.19.21\">21</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 31:23\" href=\"/Numbers.31.23\">31:23</a>."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"fig. (with allusion to cerem. usage), <em>impure thing</em>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 7:19\" href=\"/Ezekiel.7.19\">Ez 7:19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 7:20\" href=\"/Ezekiel.7.20\">20</a> (of gold), <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 1:17\" href=\"/Lamentations.1.17\">La 1:17</a> (of Jerus.); of idolatry, immorality, etc., <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 29:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.29.5\">2 Ch 29:5</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 9:11\" href=\"/Ezra.9.11\">Ezr 9:11</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(אֶרֶץ נִדָּה)</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Ezra 9:11\" href=\"/Ezra.9.11\">11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 13:1\" href=\"/Zechariah.13.1\">Zc 13:1</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(לְחַטַּאת וּלְנִדָּה)</span>."}],"num":"2."}]},"rid":"BDB06092","strong_numbers":["5079"],"next_hw":"נִידָה","prev_hw":"נְדוּד","all_cited":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["5614"],"TWOT":["1302a"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}